- R | turn both down, and go travelling on the money from the summer | v: stimulation, hedonism | mark: turned down a chance | chance: 85
- G | take it, and ask for your grandfather's old tools to start with | binds | identity | v: tradition | title: apprentice | role: men | chance: 65
- W>B | keep the college place, because the qualification will pay more in the end | v: achievement, security | mark: turned down a chance | chance: 70
- U>R | look for a trade that travels, and take a job rigging stages for touring shows | door | v: stimulation, self-direction | title: stage technician | chance: 55
- B>G | say yes only if they take your cousin on too, so you start together | v: benevolence, power | title: apprentice | role: men | chance: 50
- R>W | join the army on the spot, as you have wanted to since you were small | binds | v: security, stimulation | title: soldier | chance: 60
- G>U | work a month on site as a trial, and learn what the trade really is first | door | v: self-direction | role: men | chance: 75
works: {N} turns up on Monday to the road {N} chose, and by spring it already feels like {Ns} own.
works: The choice opens into a craft, a wage and a way of being good at something.
fails: The choice sours within months, and {N} wonders what the other road would have been.
fails: The other side of the bargain falls through, and {N} has to start again from nothing.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- step 3, calls WB (cycle s3)

== the first payslip and the first rent
tier: everyday
stages: young_adult
age: 17-20
calls: WB
threshold: young adult
step: 3
once: yes
tone: mixed
life: money, home
horizon: week
roles: parent, friend, a landlord
earth: your first proper payslip lands on a Friday, the rent goes out on the Monday, and what is left in between is yours to decide
times: Most young people, once, in the first months of full-time work away from home; often at 18 to 25, as most leave home and start work then (estimate)
scene: {Ns} first proper payslip lands on a Friday, the rent goes out on the Monday, and for the first time the sum in between is nobody's business but {Ns}.
