scene U: {N} opens a spreadsheet and starts logging every coin, curious where money actually goes when nobody else is paying.
scene B: Rent is dead money, {N} thinks, reading the landlord's name on the statement. The trick is to be the name on somebody else's statement.
scene R: Money in the account, a Friday night and a city full of bars: {N} feels rich for exactly as long as it lasts.
scene G: {parent} rings to ask whether {N} is eating properly. {N} looks into a fridge that holds a lemon and half a pint of milk.
- W | pay the rent and the bills first, and live on whatever is left | habit | v: security, conformity | self_control: + | chance: 85
- U | log every penny for a month, then set a budget that actually works | habit | v: self-direction, security | self_control: + | chance: 85
- B | put a slice of every payslip into investments from the first month, untouchable | habit | v: power, achievement | grants: savings | self_control: + | chance: 80
- R | spend the whole first payslip in one glorious weekend | habit | v: hedonism | self_control: - | chance: 92
- G | send a little home every month, as your parents once did for theirs | habit | binds | v: tradition, benevolence | self_control: + | chance: 75
- W>R | save for three months, then take the trip you promised yourself | v: hedonism, self-direction | self_control: + | act: save for three months, then take the trip they promised themselves | chance: 65
- U>G | learn to cook properly from scratch, so a little money feeds you all week | v: security, self-direction | mark: learned a skill | act: learn to cook properly from scratch, so a little money feeds them all week | chance: 85
- B>W | do the landlord's small repairs in exchange for a lower rent | v: security, power | chance: 65
- R>U | on impulse, pay a term up front for the evening class you always wanted | door | v: self-direction, stimulation | self_control: + | chance: 80
- G>B | furnish the room from skips and family attics, and bank what you save | v: security, power | closed: law: taking from skips without asking; backfire: a row with the owner, or the police at the door | chance: 75
