- U | take it home, question every clause, and only then sign | v: self-direction, security | grants: workplace pension | chance: 90
- B | use the offer to ask for more money and a better title | v: power, achievement | chance: 60
- R | turn it down; you are not ready to be pinned to one desk for life | v: self-direction | mark: turned down a chance | act: turn it down, since they are not ready to be pinned to one desk for life | chance: 80
- G | sign it, and tell the family the wandering years are over | v: security, tradition | grants: workplace pension | chance: 85
- W>B | sign, and report the colleague who fiddles expenses, now that you are safe | v: conformity, power | closed: approval: informing on a colleague; backfire: the office closes ranks | chance: 60
- U>R | sign only if they let you work from wherever you like two days a week | v: self-direction | act: sign only if they agree to remote work, from anywhere, two days a week | tech: remote work | chance: 50
- B>G | sign, and use the steady pay to get a mortgage near your family | binds | v: security, tradition | chance: 65
- R>W | sign on the spot with a whoop, in front of the whole office | v: achievement, conformity | chance: 90
- G>U | ask the oldest hand in the office what the job is really like after ten years | v: tradition, self-direction | chance: 80
works: The decision is made, and it feels like {Ns} own.
works: The new footing is solid, and {N} finds the steadiness more freeing than feared.
fails: The terms turn out worse than they looked, and {N} learns it only after signing.
fails: The offer is withdrawn before Friday, and {N} is back where {N} started.

