times: Most adults whose parents are living, once, the first time they host their parents in their own home; often in their twenties, soon after a first home of their own (estimate)
scene: For the first time {Ns} parents come to dinner at {Ns} own place. {N} has been cooking for two days, and the table has borrowed chairs round it.
scene W: {N} sets the table the way it was set at home on Sundays: the good glasses, the napkins, a seat at the head. Then {N} hesitates over whose seat that is now.
scene U: {N} has planned the evening like a project: a menu tested twice, the timings on a card by the oven, a few topics in reserve in case the talk dries up.
scene B: This is {Ns} home, {Ns} food and {Ns} rules. For one evening {parent} is the guest, and {N} means to enjoy it.
scene R: The sauce has split, the doorbell has gone, and {N} is laughing at the stove, flushed and happy and terrified.
scene G: {parent} brings a dish from home anyway, the one {N} grew up on, and sets it on the table beside {Ns} own cooking.
- W | set a proper table, toast your parents, and serve them first | v: tradition, benevolence | chance: 90
- U | serve the dish you spent months perfecting, and explain each course | v: achievement | chance: 78
- B | show them round, the flat, the job, everything you have made of yourself | identity | v: power, achievement | act: show them round, the flat, the job, everything they have made of themselves | chance: 90
- R | abandon the recipe halfway and cook by feel, laughing with them in the kitchen | v: hedonism, benevolence | chance: 80
- G | ask your parent to teach you the family dish at your own stove | v: tradition | act: ask their parent to teach them the family dish at their own stove | chance: 85
- W>B | set out, kindly, the new house rules: visits by invitation from now on | v: power, security | chance: 60
- U>R | ask them, glass in hand, the questions about their marriage you never dared ask | v: self-direction, stimulation | chance: 70
- B>G | ask your parents for help with a deposit, over the second bottle | binds | v: security, power | chance: 60
- R>W | stand up, a little drunk, and tell your parents what they did right | v: benevolence | chance: 80
- G>U | bring out the old photo albums and get them telling the family stories | v: tradition | chance: 80
works: The evening goes long and warm, and {parent} says something on the doorstep that {N} will keep.
works: For the first time {N} sees {Ns} parents as guests, and they see {N} as a host.
fails: An old argument arrives with the dessert, and the evening ends early.
fails: The food fails and the talk stalls, and {N} washes up alone afterwards, feeling about twelve years old.
